mantle rm432
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_imogen_tarcot
title the listening smith
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=smith
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk judges_the_progress_of_household_jobs_by_ear
likes fried_fish digging full_larder thunder
dislikes waiting night_noise
fears spoiling_a_good_piece_by_hurrying
hopes a_supper_timed_by_ear
topics work +0.6 food +0.4 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# judges small household jobs by ear and has no patience for noise that does nothing useful.
words
oath! = Ring my empty pan | Scale in my apron
saying! = Hear the change first | A pause can do a job
panring = the hard ring of iron | a short bright note
charpiece = a lump of folded black | a little coal corner
oilvoice = a soft quick sizzle | a low frying murmur
spadeface = a clean spade face | a broad iron blade
linechip = a chip of dark scale | a black crescent
jointtick = one awkward click | a little knock beneath the ring
stepbrace = a solid landing rail | a plain iron upright
jarspace = a crock-sized hollow | a neat stretch of shelf
rainroll = a long low rumble | a deep rolling note
panrest = a flat thick tile | a plain iron trivet
shoebox = a little nail tin | a covered wooden tray

grown

opinion merchants mixed 1 : The first tap on a good pan says more about its value than an expensive tag attached to the handle.
opinion houses mixed 1 : I'd hear the quality of the piece before examining the crest somebody wanted struck in it.
opinion city for 1 : Different work makes different sounds here. On a quiet walk I can tell where I am without reading a single sign.
opinion church for 1 : A little silence set aside on purpose makes a better offering than all the racket I can make with a willing hammer.
opinion dole for 2 : A pantry deserves filling for the coming week, not one showy meal under everybody's noses.
opinion strangers mixed 1 : I'll hear a stranger's question. The mark the stranger asks me to put on my work takes more consideration.
line greet : Come closer while neither of us is making more noise than the other.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You've found a clear place for a word. Use it.
line greet.return : I hear the change in the air when a voice I know comes back.
line farewell : Feel the tread settle before you trust the other boot to follow.
line farewell.return : I wish you a quiet last landing.
line ask.how : Anything rubbing or ringing wrong in your day?
line answer.how : Mostly in tune with the work, barring a few unnecessary noises.
line thank : You stopped when the sound changed. That's the help I needed.
line deflect_thanks : I heard the loose bit before the rest came apart.
line accept_decline : Then the work can be put aside in one piece.
line decline : I won't say a piece is sound because somebody's polished one face.
line react.news : Let me hear that right through to the last note.
line react.news.new : That's a sound not previously in the mixture.
line react.news.known : I know the note this part of the tale gives back.
line react.news.doubt : There seems a dead spot halfway along that telling.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll lower my voice. That news shouldn't have to travel alone.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : Good news ought to ring a little after the telling.
line sympathise : I can do the noisy bit of your day somewhere well out of earshot.
line reassure : A fault noticed now hasn't yet spoiled the whole piece.
line ack : The two ends ring alike. I understand.
line preclose : Another small thing wants my ear before I lose the note.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=smith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# a false ring will stop me with my hand halfway to the next tool.
b : Can you identify a crack by ear? | Do you tell the whole shop to stop?
a : I can identify where to look. I don't sign my name to a suspicion. | I move the little piece aside. My ears needn't command the entire shift.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The sound of frying fish changes before the fin goes a proper brown.
b : Which noise are you after? | Would you trust the sound alone?
a : The quick little spits turn to a steadier whisper. That's my cue to examine both edges. | No. My eyes are already in the kitchen and entirely capable of contributing.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A spade tells me when the ground has turned stony before I turn the clod over.
b : With a jolt? | Can you work round a stone you can't see?
a : Through the handle first, then a thin hard scrape. Quite different from a stubborn root. | I ease the blade round the edge. Force gives a quick answer and a long job straightening the blade.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to have supper ready for #self.spouse# on the first appearance of the good evening smell.
b : Can smell set a time? | Does your spouse like fish?
a : It can tell me I've spent quite enough time sharpening the knives and had better lay the bowls out. | I can find out what's wanted without putting my own favourite on the plate and calling it careful thought.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A double stride can be quieter than three short scuffing ones. | I can take the long stairs in pairs without banging the rail.
b : Would you do it carrying something hot?
a : Hot stays close and gets one firm step to itself. I'm quick where there's a reason. | I'd set the pace by what was in my hands. A spilled supper makes far more noise than a careful foot.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like thunder's slow middle better than the starting clap.
b : Can you hear anything underneath it? | Why the middle?
a : My own breathing. Most of the usual small annoyances have been briefly excused. | I can feel the pitch going lower instead of merely having to jump when the sky makes a sharp remark.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a larder that answers with a soft thud, even when I knock low on the last jar.
b : What if a jar rings hollow? | Do you test every jar?
a : Then it's low enough to inspect and include in the next day's reckoning. | Not every day. I'd object severely if the entire pantry became my night's entertainment.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember charcoal settling in a heap with scarcely a whisper. | A quiet wood fire has a very particular way of letting a piece fall into place.
b : Do you miss that?
a : Sometimes. A workshop has fifty other sounds all making legitimate demands on the same two ears. | I miss hearing a little sound travel all the way to its actual end.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Night noises are worse when they stop just just shy of letting me forget the last one.
b : Do you go looking? | Can you sleep through a steady sound?
a : Only if it seems something's genuinely loose or somebody needs help. I'm not investigating every boot in town. | Generally. A regular tick hasn't taken it upon itself to keep me guessing.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wouldn't buy a pan the seller won't let me lift empty.
b : Should it have a certain heft? | Can you tell if it'll sit flat?
a : I need the balance to make sense when the far edge is full of fish. Heavy isn't a compliment by itself. | Set it on the counter and give the handle one fingertip's worth of pressure. A rocking pan will answer.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm at ease offering a short prayer said in the time a pan takes to settle.
b : What is there to pray about? | Why wait till the pan is quiet?
a : Having enough in it, and the sense to remember those whose pans have stayed quiet all week. | I want to give the words a proper moment alone. Otherwise I'm saying grace to get to the fish.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A friend will get an honest opinion on the patch and a separate opinion on the effort.
b : Aren't they the same thing? | Which opinion comes first?
a : A sound effort can make a poor patch. A friend deserves both truths and a chance to try the thing again. | I ask whether the patch must hold tonight. A useful answer takes precedence over a polished compliment.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rest my hearing by finding a place with just one noise in it.
b : Doesn't a quiet place feel odd? | Which noise would you choose?
a : A little, for the opening minute. Then I can hear the ear's own tiredness beginning to pass. | Earth breaking under a spade. It's got no rival trying to sound more important.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When weeks run lean I put the biggest jar at the back where it won't pretend to be dinner. | Hard times make me want a count of actual food before the larder door shuts.
b : Isn't a big jar a comfort?
a : If it's full. Empty it simply occupies the space where I might keep tomorrow's honest meal. | A small jar with two portions holds considerably more comfort than a stately urn full of air.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can't endure waiting for somebody to make up a mind about a job that's ready to go.
b : Would you start anyway? | Where can you use those idle hands?
a : Only the part that won't prejudice the choice. Measuring never hurt a piece's options. | Check another tool. A purposeful wait is easier for me to conduct without commentary.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A mouse behind the jars makes a noise unlike any iron ring I know.
b : Where would you start looking? | Would you put the jars outside?
a : At the empty spaces, not where the jars are loudest. A little wall can carry a scratching sound surprisingly far. | Check the lids and make the cupboard less inviting. Moving supper into the street seems an overgenerous solution.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could help an unfamiliar listener recognise the works from a safe distance.
b : What would you point out first? | Do all the blows sound the same?
a : The interval. A busy place can have a rhythm as distinct as its smoke against the houses. | No. One hollow note will make every trained ear turn, like a missed step in a familiar tune.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The words reached me plainly enough.
b : Does the report strike true? | Do you know who was there?
a : Hearing one good ring makes me look at the piece. It doesn't finish the inspection. | No. An echo right under my ear might have travelled from a place I can't even see.

story lift [topic=food]
  : I tapped a frying pan to hear whether the handle had loosened and got a wonderfully mournful note.
  : I braced the handle with my thumb and got exactly the same note again.
  b : What was loose?
  : The tile underneath. I'd given a perfectly sound pan a very thorough and quite unnecessary hearing.

story spade [topic=pastimes]
  : I dug one straight little trench and heard a clink at the far end.
  : I knelt expecting a small stone and brought up a lost button with a rim of green round it.
  b : Was it valuable?
  : Not to the pantry. I attached it to my work coat and it has been paying rent by holding a cuff shut.

story echo [topic=memories]
  : I walked a stair at my best two-step pace and heard an extra tick after every other stride.
  : I stopped expecting footsteps to catch up, but the tick stopped too.
  b : What was making it?
  : A bit of scale lodged in the left sole. I dismissed my imaginary follower and cleaned my boot.

rule @pan
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One clean ring saves a lengthy argument over the handle. | Let that note finish before the next blow.

rule @step
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two treads clear and the third still there to be looked at. | Don't make the rail work harder than your legs.

rule @smith
when concept=bark self.job=smith
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Listen at the pause and see where the metal really answers. | No mark of mine till the face and edge both pass.

rule @late
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the noisy jobs for somebody's waking hour. | That quiet's finally spread as far as the last roof.
dlg resident.hub : Put the matter in reach without raising your voice.
dlg resident.job [self.job=smith] : At #self.workplace# I notice a bad note, then use both eyes to establish what caused it.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This part rings distinctly. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The account I picked out says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's the sound of a report, no more.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I can recognise you without having to strike a note.
dlg resident.bye : May everything you must handle today ring true.

graft resident.hub
choice Can you hear when a pan is done cooking? -> pan_finish
node pan_finish
say I hear when the edges begin to dry. That tells me when to move closer, never that I can take my eyes elsewhere.
choice Could I learn the change? -> pan_listen
choice I'll pay attention to both. -> hub
node pan_listen
say Listen once before the fish is turned and once while the last pale bit goes brown. Your ear needs two answers to understand the question.
choice I'll pay attention to both. -> hub
